(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #111. `L's first` and `L's last` reading out a nested
 collection hand back a copy, the same as `element N of L`.)

a list called a1 is [1, 2].
a list called a2 is [3, 4].
a list called outer is [a1, a2].
a list called first_got is outer's first.
a list called last_got is outer's last.
Set element 1 of first_got to 101.
Set element 1 of last_got to 303.
print outer.
print first_got.
print last_got.
